    "# Environment Setup for Model Optimization\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook will guide you through setting up your environment for the model optimization workshop. We'll install necessary packages and configure AWS credentials."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Install Required Packages\n",
    "\n",
    "We've provided a `requirements.txt` file with all the necessary packages. Let's install them:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install -q -r requirements.txt"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Verify Installations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "import transformers\n",
    "import boto3\n",
    "import sagemaker\n",
    "import optimum\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"PyTorch version: {torch.__version__}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Transformers version: {transformers.__version__}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Boto3 version: {boto3.__version__}\")\n",
    "print(f\"SageMaker SDK version: {sagemaker.__version__}\")\n",
    "# Note: optimum doesn't have a __version__ attribute\n",
    "print(f\"Optimum installed: {'Yes' if 'optimum' in locals() else 'No'}\")\n",
    "print(f\"CUDA available: {torch.cuda.is_available()}\")"
   ]
  }
    "\n",
    "print(f\"PyTorch version: {torch.__version__}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Transformers version: {transformers.__version__}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Boto3 version: {boto3.__version__}\")\n",
    "print(f\"SageMaker SDK version: {sagemaker.__version__}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Optimum version: {optimum.__version__}\")\n",
    "print(f\"CUDA available: {torch.cuda.is_available()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Configure AWS Region and Get Execution Role\n",
    "\n",
    "When running in SageMaker, we'll use the execution role assigned to the notebook instance. This role has the necessary permissions to interact with AWS services."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sagemaker\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get the SageMaker session\n",
    "sagemaker_session = sagemaker.Session()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get the execution role\n",
    "role = sagemaker.get_execution_role()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get the AWS region\n",
    "region = boto3.session.Session().region_name\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"SageMaker execution role: {role}\")\n",
    "print(f\"AWS region: {region}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Let's verify that our AWS credentials are working:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Verify AWS credentials\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    client = boto3.client('sts')\n",
    "    response = client.get_caller_identity()\n",
    "    print(f\"AWS credentials verified. Account ID: {response['Account']}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Role ARN: {response['Arn']}\")\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Error verifying AWS credentials: {e}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Create S3 Bucket for Workshop\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll create an S3 bucket to store our models and data. We'll use a unique name based on the account ID."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import boto3\n",
    "import uuid\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generate a unique bucket name\n",
    "account_id = boto3.client('sts').get_caller_identity().get('Account')\n",
    "bucket_name = f\"model-optimization-workshop-{account_id}-{uuid.uuid4().hex[:8]}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create the bucket\n",
    "s3_client = boto3.client('s3')\n",
    "region = boto3.session.Session().region_name\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    if region == 'us-east-1':\n",
    "        s3_client.create_bucket(Bucket=bucket_name)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        s3_client.create_bucket(\n",
    "            Bucket=bucket_name,\n",
    "            CreateBucketConfiguration={'LocationConstraint': region}\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    print(f\"Created S3 bucket: {bucket_name}\")\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Error creating S3 bucket: {e}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save the bucket name for later use\n",
    "import os\n",
    "os.environ['WORKSHOP_BUCKET'] = bucket_name\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create a file to store the bucket name\n",
    "with open('workshop_config.py', 'w') as f:\n",
    "    f.write(f\"S3_BUCKET = '{bucket_name}'\\n\")\n",
    "    f.write(f\"AWS_REGION = '{region}'\\n\")\n",
    "    f.write(f\"SAGEMAKER_ROLE_ARN = '{role}'\\n\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Create Workshop Configuration"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create workshop configuration file\n",
    "with open('workshop_config.py', 'w') as f:\n",
    "    f.write(f\"S3_BUCKET = '{bucket_name}'\\n\")\n",
    "    f.write(f\"AWS_REGION = '{region}'\\n\")\n",
    "    f.write(f\"SAGEMAKER_ROLE_ARN = '{role}'\\n\")"
   ]
  },
  {
